WEBVTT - Orbit Product Tour Captions

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
What if a startup could be built with an AI founding team?

2
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:29.500
Welcome to Orbit, the AI Founder Operating System transforming ideas into real, shipping products.

3
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Chapter 2: Creating Startup Mission. We initiate an AI Interview Preparation Platform.

4
00:00:48.500 --> 00:01:14.500
Orbit initializes mission control, allocating dedicated compute and preparing 15 autonomous agents.

5
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Chapter 3: Problem Discovery. The agent parses candidate anxiety, lack of actionable feedback, and interview barriers.

6
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:44.500
Simulated evidence synthesis isolates the core wedge: real-time voice-driven mock interviews with instant rubric scoring.

7
00:01:45.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Chapter 4: Market Research. The Market Agent sizes the opportunity: 18.4 billion dollar TAM with 650 million dollar obtainable market.

8
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:29.500
Benchmarking existing incumbents highlights our defensible moat: low-latency speech reasoning and personalized coaching.

9
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Chapter 5: Product Strategy. Translating research into decisive MVP scope, user personas, and a ruthless 80/20 feature priority list.

10
00:02:52.500 --> 00:03:14.500
Clear product boundaries protect runway and ensure rapid validation within our target market segment.

11
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Chapter 6: UI/UX Architect. Establishing component hierarchy, cosmic dark design tokens, and high-fidelity candidate dashboard wireframes.

12
00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:59.500
Responsive layouts and WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility guidelines are codified directly into actionable frontend tokens.

13
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:22.000
Chapter 7: Technical Architect. Formulating production-grade PostgreSQL DDL schemas, OpenAPI 3.1 REST contracts, and async WebSockets topology.

14
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:44.500
Zero-downtime indexes, connection pooling, and sub-100ms audio stream processing budgets are locked in.

15
00:04:45.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Chapter 8: Sprint Planner. Turning architectural specifications into two-week agile Kanban sprints.

16
00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:14.500
Every backlog ticket includes clear acceptance criteria, test cases, and a rigorous definition of done.

17
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Chapter 9: Gemini Co-Founder. Founder asks: What should I build first?

18
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:59.500
Gemini evaluates trade-offs, warns against building complex question banks before validating WebRTC voice latency, and outlines immediate next actions.

19
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:22.000
Chapter 10: Startup Blueprint. All 15 specialist outputs converge into one unified, investor-ready PRD, schema, and API bundle.

20
00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:44.500
The entire startup vision is structured and exportable as living engineering documentation.

21
00:06:45.000 --> 00:07:00.000
Chapter 11: Launch Center. Pre-flight verification audits security headers, SSL certificates, and zero-day rollback triggers.

22
00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:14.500
94 percent launch readiness achieved. Infrastructure is cleared for production traffic.

23
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:30.000
Chapter 12: Closing. From Idea To Product. Powered By Orbit.
